        <div class="fc-delta-reason">Sunday cold-start audit: p_inherited=0.35, p_cold=0.53, gap=18pp — FLAG applied. Two material developments since last reasoning (May 19): (1) the coalition's own dissolution bill passed 110-0 preliminary reading May 20 — an institutional action, the mechanism is now in motion; (2) polling (Times of Israel May 19-20) shows the pro-Netanyahu bloc at only 49-51 seats, 10 seats short of majority. <em>Judge calibration (+5pp from Analyst's 0.52 → 0.57; DA opposing narrative partially rejected):</em> DA argued the 110-0 vote is procedural (Netanyahu controls House Committee scheduling) and wartime-coalition-tolerance reduces the historical 80%+ collapse rate. Judge partially rejects: the structural arithmetic — 49-51 seats vs. 61 needed — is not a procedural artefact, and the wartime-tolerance haircut was already overapplied at Analyst's 0.52. DA's falsifier (Degel HaTorah–Netanyahu side-deal on Haredi bill by May 31) is logged as the primary watchlist item for next Sunday's review. Historical base rate: Israeli coalitions with sub-55-seat effective blocs and in-process dissolution bills collapse in >80% of cases; 5-month window and institutional resilience tempering applied. Judge selects 0.57.</div>
        <dl class="fc-meta-row">
          <dt>Resolution</dt><dd>YES if Knesset roll-call vote confirms coalition loss of majority (61 seats), OR if Netanyahu announces early dissolution and election date moves earlier than 2026-10-27. NO if coalition survives to mandatory election date with 61+ seats intact.</dd>
          <dt>Sources OK</dt><dd>Knesset official record + Reuters/Haaretz/Times of Israel confirmation. Polling alone does not resolve.</dd>
          <dt>Ambiguity</dt><dd>If coalition drops below 61 but Netanyahu remains caretaker PM until election: counts as YES (majority lost). Smotrich departure while coalition retains 61+: counts as NO. Dissolution bill passing all three readings: counts as YES at that point. Reviewed weekly (Sundays) only; no intra-week deltas.</dd>
        </dl>
