      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (36%):</strong> MOU signed at principal level but Hormuz operational restart lags June 10 (F1 resolves NO on timing), coalition dissolution stalls via Haredi side-deal (F4 remains unresolved), and the region settles into a monitored-standoff equilibrium through summer.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (42%):</strong> Dual-principal confirmation (Trump + Iranian principal) closes F2 YES; N1 formalized via MOU ceasefire clause; Netanyahu coalition collapse (F4) reshuffles Israeli war-cabinet toward centrist government — P(F2) × P(N1|F2) drives scenario probability. Scenario probability shifted down 13pp from Analyst's 55% on Judge's calibrated F2 reduction.</p>
