  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · 200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media on May 23-24 ran a split message. IRNA — the official government wire — quoted an unnamed spokesperson acknowledging that "the trend has been toward narrowing differences," the most conciliatory language from the state apparatus in several weeks. This formulation is careful: it does not name a deal, does not confirm the Axios MOU terms, and cannot be read as principal-level confirmation for resolution purposes under <span class="cite">F2</span>. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span> without move</p>
      <p>IRGC-linked Fars News took the opposing line: Trump's "largely negotiated" announcement was framed as "propaganda justifying American retreat," not Iranian concession. Tasnim ran no confirmation of the MOU terms. This IRGC media posture is consistent with the documented pattern of the Revolutionary Guard blocking President Pezeshkian from key decisions — ISW and US intelligence assessments as of April 2026 noted IRGC commander Vahidi and Parliament Speaker Ghalibaf as the effective decision gate, with Pezeshkian sidelined. Ghalibaf's reported approval of the MOU draft (Axios) is therefore the more authoritative Iranian signal than Pezeshkian's public statements. → supports <span class="cite">F2</span> without move</p>
      <p>Mojtaba Khamenei — selected as Supreme Leader by the Assembly of Experts in March after the death of his father — has not been seen or heard from publicly since assuming the role, per Iran International. ISW assessed he may have been incapacitated in the same strike. The constitutional vacuum at the top of the Iranian state is the structural variable most resistant to OSINT observation; its resolution trajectory is underdetermined. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

